course: dictionary
lesson: 11464
title: Words of promise and rules
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Adultery is a noun. It means a married person having a loving, romantic or sexual relationship with someone who is not their husband or wife. You will meet it in Bible lessons and religious education.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «One of the Ten Commandments says: You shall not commit adultery.» A commandment is a rule that must be obeyed, so adultery is something people are told not to do.
explain: The word is about marriage, which is a promise. A marriage promise is to be faithful, which means staying loyal to one partner. When that promise is broken, the word tells you what has happened.
fact: Adultery is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "adulteries".
fact: «Commit adultery» is a common phrase. It means to do adultery.
fact: Adultery is one of the sins named in the Ten Commandments in the Bible.
fact: Christians believe marriage is a lifelong promise of faithfulness, so adultery breaks that promise.
exercise: What does adultery mean? | Being very hungry after a long day | A rule about school dinners | Making a promise to a friend | *A married person having a romantic relationship with someone who is not their husband or wife
exercise: Which word means a rule that must be obeyed? | Whisper | *Commandment | Breakfast | Lesson
exercise: In «Christians believe marriage is a lifelong promise of faithfulness», what does faithfulness mean? | Forgetting promises on purpose | Being very tall | Eating breakfast slowly | *Staying loyal to one partner
test: «The Bible says: you shall not commit adultery.» What does commit adultery mean? | Break a promise to keep a secret | Tell a lie about your age | Forget your homework | *Have a romantic relationship outside marriage while you are married
test: Which sentence about adultery is true? | It is a countable noun, so we can say many adulteries | It is the name of a church | *It is an uncountable noun, so it has no plural | It is a type of food
exam: Why does adultery break a marriage promise? | Because it means being loyal to one partner | *Because it means being unfaithful to your husband or wife | Because it means having a birthday | Because it means going to school every day
